Must not touch: files under `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`, `crates/`, or other apps. Governed by CLAUDE.md rules 3, 7 and 9, R2122000 (minimum 44px tap targets for controls), R1581000 (menus fit one screen), and issue #3219 (button roles).

## Steps

### Step 1: Create `apps/web/src/tabs/Tabs.tsx`
Create `Tabs.tsx` adhering to the WAI-ARIA tabs pattern:
- Types:
  ```tsx
  export type TabItem<T extends string = string> = {
    id: T;
    label: ReactNode;
    testId?: string;
    className?: string;
    disabled?: boolean;
    panel?: ReactNode;
    panelTestId?: string;
    panelClassName?: string;
    panelAs?: "div" | "section";
  };

  export type TabsProps<T extends string = string> = {
    items: readonly TabItem<T>[];
    value: T;
    onChange: (value: T) => void;
    label: string;
    testId?: string;
    idPrefix: string;
    className?: string;
    tablistClassName?: string;
    tabClassName?: string;
    panelsClassName?: string;
    panelsRef?: Ref<HTMLDivElement>;
    keepMounted?: boolean;
    panelAs?: "div" | "section";
  };
  ```
- Component `Tabs<T extends string = string>({ ... }: TabsProps<T>)`:
  - Maintains `tabRefs = useRef<Map<T, HTMLButtonElement>>(new Map())`.
  - Computes `activeItem = items.find((item) => item.id === value) ?? items[0]`.
  - Keyboard handler `onTabKeyDown`:
    - Reads enabled tab items: `const enabled = items.filter((item) => !item.disabled)`.
    - Finds current index: `at = enabled.findIndex((item) => item.id === (activeItem?.id ?? value))`.
    - Handles keys:
      - `ArrowRight`: `(at + 1) % enabled.length`
      - `ArrowLeft`: `(at - 1 + enabled.length) % enabled.length`
      - `Home`: `0`
      - `End`: `enabled.length - 1`
    - When handled, calls `event.preventDefault()`, invokes `onChange(nextItem.id)`, and focuses `tabRefs.current.get(nextItem.id)`.
  - Renders `<div className={`tabs ${className ?? ""}`.trim()}>`:
    - Tablist: `<div role="tablist" aria-label={label} data-testid={testId} className={`tabs__tablist ${tablistClassName ?? ""}`.trim()} onKeyDown={onTabKeyDown}>`.
    - Tab buttons:
      - `type="button"`, `role="tab"`
      - `id={`${idPrefix}-tab-${item.id}`}`
      - `aria-controls={`${idPrefix}-panel-${item.id}`}`
      - `aria-selected={item.id === value}`
      - `tabIndex={item.id === value ? 0 : -1}` (roving tabindex)
      - `className={`tabs__tab ${tabClassName ?? ""} ${item.className ?? ""}`.trim()}`
      - `data-testid={item.testId}`
      - `disabled={item.disabled}`
      - `onClick={() => onChange(item.id)}`
      - `ref={(node) => { if (node === null) tabRefs.current.delete(item.id); else tabRefs.current.set(item.id, node); }}`
    - Panels (if any `item.panel` is defined):
      - If `panelsClassName` or `panelsRef` is provided, wraps inside `<div className={panelsClassName} ref={panelsRef}>`.
      - If `keepMounted`: renders all items where `item.panel` is defined, with `hidden={item.id !== value}`.
      - If not `keepMounted`: renders only the panel for `activeItem` when `activeItem.panel` is defined.
      - Panel element: `const PanelTag = item.panelAs ?? (panelAs ?? "div")` with:
        - `id={`${idPrefix}-panel-${item.id}`}`
        - `role="tabpanel"`
        - `aria-labelledby={`${idPrefix}-tab-${item.id}`}`
        - `data-testid={item.panelTestId}`
        - `className={item.panelClassName}`
        - `hidden={keepMounted ? item.id !== value : undefined}`
- Imports `./tabs.css`.

### Step 2: Create `apps/web/src/tabs/Segmented.tsx`
Create `Segmented.tsx`:
- Types:
  ```tsx
  export type SegmentOption<T extends string = string> = {
    value: T;
    label: ReactNode;
    testId?: string;
    className?: string;
    disabled?: boolean;
    title?: string;
  };

  export type SegmentedProps<T extends string = string> = {
    options: readonly SegmentOption<T>[];
    value: T;
    onChange: (value: T) => void;
    label: string;
    testId?: string;
    className?: string;
    itemClassName?: string;
    disabled?: boolean;
  };
  ```
- Component `Segmented<T extends string = string>`:
  - Maintains `btnRefs = useRef<Map<T, HTMLButtonElement>>(new Map())`.
  - Arrow key navigation `onKeyDown`:
    - Handles `ArrowRight` and `ArrowLeft` among non-disabled options, wrapping boundaries, focusing the target button and calling `onChange(nextOption.value)`.
  - Renders `<div role="group" aria-label={label} data-testid={testId} className={`segmented ${className ?? ""}`.trim()} onKeyDown={onKeyDown}>`:
    - For each option:
      - `<button type="button" role="button" aria-pressed={option.value === value} data-testid={option.testId} title={option.title} disabled={disabled || option.disabled} className={`segmented__item ${option.value === value ? "segmented__item--selected" : ""} ${itemClassName ?? ""} ${option.className ?? ""}`.trim()} onClick={() => onChange(option.value)} ref={(node) => { if (node === null) btnRefs.current.delete(option.value); else btnRefs.current.set(option.value, node); }}>`
- Imports `./tabs.css`.

### Step 3: Create `apps/web/src/tabs/tabs.css`
Create `tabs.css` compliant with design tokens (palette, spacing, surfaces, typescale, button roles):
- Use tokens ONLY (zero raw hex/rgb literals, zero raw px spacing, zero raw border-radii):
  ```css
  /* Tabs and Segmented component styling (#3222), taking selected looks from button roles (#3219). */

  .tabs {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .tabs__tablist {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-1);
    overflow-x: auto;
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
    scrollbar-width: none;
  }

  .tabs__tablist::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }

  .tabs__tab {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    min-width: var(--hit-min);
    min-height: var(--hit-min);
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0 0;
    background: none;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--type-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: nowrap;
    cursor: var(--cursor-glove-point, pointer);
  }

  .tabs__tab:hover:not(:disabled) {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .tabs__tab[aria-selected="true"] {
    border-bottom-color: var(--selected);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .tabs__tab:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--selected);
    outline-offset: -2px;
  }

  /* Segmented one-of-n toggle buttons */
  .segmented {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .segmented__item {
    min-height: var(--hit-min);
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-bright);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: var(--type-sm);
    white-space: nowrap;
    cursor: var(--cursor-glove-point, pointer);
  }

  .segmented__item:hover:not(:disabled, [aria-disabled="true"]) {
    border-color: var(--text-dim);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg-raised) 70%, var(--line-bright));
  }

  .segmented__item[aria-pressed="true"] {
    border-color: var(--selected);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--selected) 12%, var(--bg-raised));
    color: var(--text);
  }

  /* Shared filter <select> style with touch minimum height (R2122000) */
  .select-filter,
  .stats-select,
  .dungeon-stats__select {
    min-height: var(--hit-min);
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-bright);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: var(--type-sm);
  }
  ```

