# Plan (gemini-3.8-flash-high, medium)

## Goal
Implement a unified `Tabs` component and a unified `Segmented` component with a single shared stylesheet (`tabs.css`) for menus' tabs and filter controls across the web app. Migrate `SettingsPanel` and statistics views (`/stats`) to `Tabs`, giving `stats` full WAI-ARIA arrow key navigation, roving tabindex, and panel association; migrate the leaderboard ladder toggle, stats view toggle, and collection payment options to `Segmented`, eliminating the use of `button-primary` for selected segments; standardize `<select>` filters with shared touch targets of `min-height: var(--hit-min)` (R2122000); and document why true multi-selects and long select dropdowns stay as-is.

## Files to touch

| File path | Type | Changes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `apps/web/src/tabs/Tabs.tsx` | new | Unified `Tabs` component with `role="tablist"`, roving `tabindex`, Left/Right/Home/End keyboard handling, `aria-selected`, `aria-controls`, and panel mounting. |
| `apps/web/src/tabs/Segmented.tsx` | new | Unified `Segmented` toggle component with `role="group"`, `aria-pressed`, keyboard arrow navigation, and button role styling. |
| `apps/web/src/tabs/tabs.css` | new | Shared stylesheet for `Tabs`, `Segmented`, and shared select filters. |
| `apps/web/src/tabs/index.ts` | new | Re-exports `Tabs`, `Segmented`, and their types. |
| `apps/web/src/tabs/Tabs.test.tsx` | new | Unit tests for `Tabs` covering WAI-ARIA roles, attributes, arrow keys, Home/End, roving tabindex, and change callbacks. |
| `apps/web/src/tabs/Segmented.test.tsx` | new | Unit tests for `Segmented` covering group role, `aria-pressed` state reflection, keyboard navigation, disabled options, and change callbacks. |
| `apps/web/src/settings/SettingsPanel.tsx` | change | Replace manual tablist implementation with `Tabs`, preserving `settings-tablist`, `settings-tab-${id}`, `settings-section-${id}`, and `settings-body` ref. |
| `apps/web/src/routes/stats.tsx` | change | Replace manual tabs with `Tabs` (adding arrow key navigation) and replace Table/Grid view toggle with `Segmented`. |
| `apps/web/src/routes/leaderboard.tsx` | change | Replace manual ladder buttons with `Segmented`, removing `button-primary` from selected ladder segment. |
| `apps/web/src/collection/LooksScreen.tsx` | change | Replace payment ways button row (`collection-looks__ways`) with `Segmented`. |
| `apps/web/src/routes/stats.css` | change | Remove redundant local `.stats-tab` and `.stats-view-btn` custom styles in favor of `tabs.css`. |

Must not touch: files under `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`, `crates/`, or other apps. Governed by CLAUDE.md rules 3, 7 and 9, R2122000 (minimum 44px tap targets for controls), R1581000 (menus fit one screen), and issue #3219 (button roles).

## Steps

### Step 1: Create `apps/web/src/tabs/Tabs.tsx`
Create `Tabs.tsx` adhering to the WAI-ARIA tabs pattern:
- Types:
  ```tsx
  export type TabItem<T extends string = string> = {
    id: T;
    label: ReactNode;
    testId?: string;
    className?: string;
    disabled?: boolean;
    panel?: ReactNode;
    panelTestId?: string;
    panelClassName?: string;
    panelAs?: "div" | "section";
  };

  export type TabsProps<T extends string = string> = {
    items: readonly TabItem<T>[];
    value: T;
    onChange: (value: T) => void;
    label: string;
    testId?: string;
    idPrefix: string;
    className?: string;
    tablistClassName?: string;
    tabClassName?: string;
    panelsClassName?: string;
    panelsRef?: Ref<HTMLDivElement>;
    keepMounted?: boolean;
    panelAs?: "div" | "section";
  };
  ```
- Component `Tabs<T extends string = string>({ ... }: TabsProps<T>)`:
  - Maintains `tabRefs = useRef<Map<T, HTMLButtonElement>>(new Map())`.
  - Computes `activeItem = items.find((item) => item.id === value) ?? items[0]`.
  - Keyboard handler `onTabKeyDown`:
    - Reads enabled tab items: `const enabled = items.filter((item) => !item.disabled)`.
    - Finds current index: `at = enabled.findIndex((item) => item.id === (activeItem?.id ?? value))`.
    - Handles keys:
      - `ArrowRight`: `(at + 1) % enabled.length`
      - `ArrowLeft`: `(at - 1 + enabled.length) % enabled.length`
      - `Home`: `0`
      - `End`: `enabled.length - 1`
    - When handled, calls `event.preventDefault()`, invokes `onChange(nextItem.id)`, and focuses `tabRefs.current.get(nextItem.id)`.
  - Renders `<div className={`tabs ${className ?? ""}`.trim()}>`:
    - Tablist: `<div role="tablist" aria-label={label} data-testid={testId} className={`tabs__tablist ${tablistClassName ?? ""}`.trim()} onKeyDown={onTabKeyDown}>`.
    - Tab buttons:
      - `type="button"`, `role="tab"`
      - `id={`${idPrefix}-tab-${item.id}`}`
      - `aria-controls={`${idPrefix}-panel-${item.id}`}`
      - `aria-selected={item.id === value}`
      - `tabIndex={item.id === value ? 0 : -1}` (roving tabindex)
      - `className={`tabs__tab ${tabClassName ?? ""} ${item.className ?? ""}`.trim()}`
      - `data-testid={item.testId}`
      - `disabled={item.disabled}`
      - `onClick={() => onChange(item.id)}`
      - `ref={(node) => { if (node === null) tabRefs.current.delete(item.id); else tabRefs.current.set(item.id, node); }}`
    - Panels (if any `item.panel` is defined):
      - If `panelsClassName` or `panelsRef` is provided, wraps inside `<div className={panelsClassName} ref={panelsRef}>`.
      - If `keepMounted`: renders all items where `item.panel` is defined, with `hidden={item.id !== value}`.
      - If not `keepMounted`: renders only the panel for `activeItem` when `activeItem.panel` is defined.
      - Panel element: `const PanelTag = item.panelAs ?? (panelAs ?? "div")` with:
        - `id={`${idPrefix}-panel-${item.id}`}`
        - `role="tabpanel"`
        - `aria-labelledby={`${idPrefix}-tab-${item.id}`}`
        - `data-testid={item.panelTestId}`
        - `className={item.panelClassName}`
        - `hidden={keepMounted ? item.id !== value : undefined}`
- Imports `./tabs.css`.

